	"bugClass": {
		"id": "vault-lookup-key-mismatch",
		"title": "Vault lookup omits the site matching key",
		"cause": "A saved credential lookup uses only the requested service or entry name for equality, while the saved login is associated with a site/domain and the request omits that site identifier. This makes an existing login appear missing and can trigger an unnecessary request to save the password again.",
		"criteria": "Include a site when credential retrieval matches saved logins against a request using service/entry-name equality alone, with no site/domain/URL matching key supplied or considered. Also include when a broker or adapter drops the site/domain/URL field before forwarding a credential lookup. Either mechanism independently qualifies. Exclude cases where the request and lookup consistently use a canonical site/domain key or the item is absent for a different reason.",
